-    """Read a user ``config.yaml`` EXACTLY as written (no defaults/overlay/expansion, no cache).
+    """Read a user ``config.yaml`` EXACTLY as written (no defaults/overlay/expansion; a private copy).
     ONLY legal for write-back round-trips and raw-file diagnostics — behavioral reads must use
     load_config()/load_config_readonly()."""
     if config_path is None:
diff --git a/hermes_cli/config_backend.py b/hermes_cli/config_backend.py
index 2363fbca56..5626571149 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/config_backend.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/config_backend.py
@@ -7,8 +7,9 @@ the hermes home (profile): one multiplexed process serves N profiles, and every
 already keys on the config path, so a backend keeps per-home state.
 
 :class:`FileBackend` (the default) is today's behaviour byte for byte:
-the version is the ``file_signature`` stat tuple, reads are ``open`` + ``fast_safe_load`` and raise
-exactly what those raise (``FileNotFoundError`` for an absent file, ``OSError``, YAML errors), and
+the version is the ``file_signature`` stat tuple, reads parse with ``fast_safe_load`` (an unchanged
